@startuml F1_BettingApp_Sequence_PlaceBet

!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequence {
  BackgroundColor #FEFEFE
  BorderColor #333333
  ActorBackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  ActorBorderColor #01579B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F3E5F5
  ParticipantBorderColor #6A1B9A
  ArrowColor #333333
}

title F1 Betting Application — Sequence Diagram: Place Bet Operation\n

participant "👤 User\n(Browser)" as user
participant "🖥️ Angular SPA\n(Frontend)" as angular
participant "🌐 HTTP Client\n& Interceptor" as http
participant "🔌 API Layer\nBetsController" as api
participant "⚙️ Application Layer\nBettingService" as service
participant "✅ Validators\n(FluentValidation)" as validators
participant "📋 Domain Layer\nBet Entity" as domain
participant "🔧 Infrastructure\nBettingRepository" as repo
participant "💾 Database\n(SQL Server)" as db

autonumber

user -> angular: 1. Click "Place Bet" button
user -> angular: 2. Fill in bet details\n(Amount, Driver, Race)
angular -> http: 3. POST /api/bets\n{userId, raceId, driverId, amount}
http -> http: 4. Add JWT Token\nto headers

note over http
  HTTP Interceptor:
  • Adds Authorization header
  • Sets Content-Type
  • Handles CORS
end note

http -> api: 5. Send HTTP POST request

note over api
  BetsController:
  • Extract route params
  • Validate HTTP request
  • Map to DTO
end note

api -> api: 6. Validate JWT token\n& Extract User ID

alt Token Invalid
  api --> user: ❌ 401 Unauthorized
else Token Valid
  api -> service: 7. Call PlaceBetAsync(\n  userId, raceId,\n  driverId, amount)
  
  note over service
    BettingService:
    • Orchestrate business logic
    • Coordinate validation
    • Calculate results
  end note
  
  service -> repo: 8. GetUserByIdAsync(userId)
  repo -> db: 9. SELECT * FROM Users\nWHERE user_id = @userId
  db --> repo: 10. Return User entity
  repo --> service: 11. Return User
  
  service -> validators: 12. ValidateAsync(bet)
  
  note over validators
    Validators:
    • Check balance
    • Validate amount > 0
    • Check race hasn't started
    • Check driver exists
  end note
  
  validators -> service: 13. Return validation result
  
  alt Validation Fails
    service --> api: ❌ BadRequest\n(validation errors)
    api --> http: 14. 400 Bad Request
    http --> angular: 15. Display error message
    angular --> user: ❌ Show validation error
  else Validation Succeeds
    
    alt Insufficient Balance
      service --> api: ❌ BadRequest\n(insufficient balance)
      api --> http: 16. 400 Bad Request
      http --> angular: 17. Display error
      angular --> user: ❌ "Not enough points"
    else Sufficient Balance
      
      service -> service: 18. Create Bet entity
      note over service
        Bet object created:
        • Id (generated by DB)
        • UserId
        • RaceId
        • DriverId
        • Amount
        • Status = Pending
        • CreatedAt = Now
      end note
      
      service -> repo: 19. AddAsync(bet)
      
      repo -> domain: 20. Create new Bet instance
      note over domain
        Domain Entity:
        Validates business rules
      end note
      
      repo -> db: 21. INSERT INTO Bets\n(user_id, race_id, driver_id,\namount, status, created_at)\nVALUES (...)
      
      db -> db: 22. Execute INSERT\n& Generate ID
      db --> repo: 23. Return identity\n(bet_id)
      
      repo -> db: 24. SELECT * FROM Bets\nWHERE bet_id = @id
      db --> repo: 25. Return Bet with ID
      
      repo --> service: 26. Return created Bet
      
      service -> service: 27. Map Bet to DTO
      service --> api: 28. Return BetDto
      
      api -> api: 29. Create response object
      api --> http: 30. 201 Created\n{bet data}
      
      http -> http: 30a. Extract response data\n& Transform to JSON
      
      http --> angular: 31. Return response
      
      angular -> angular: 32. Parse JSON response
      angular -> angular: 33. Update component state
      angular -> angular: 34. Update bet history list
      
      angular --> user: ✅ "Bet placed successfully!"
      user -> user: 35. See confirmation\n& updated balance
    end
  end
end

note over bottom
  **Key Points:**
  • JWT authentication on every API call
  • Validation at multiple layers (API, Service, Entity)
  • Clean separation of concerns
  • DTOs for data transfer
  • Database constraints ensure data integrity
  • Transaction handled by Entity Framework Core
end note

@enduml
